uments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"inference\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"packet_sha256\\\":\\\"831e40ae3637bfb07c7f51e87b273f05095f75f79a7135ed8daa742433026da5\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Fresh review used the complete frozen packet.json (all 577 lines) and the declared Yui Audit A, self-containment, and format rules; no source proof, other inference body, prior review, or additional mathematical task material was used. The permitted calculations expressly cover divided-power iteration, localization/reduction of free modules, and elementary ideal calculations in Z_(p). The formulas, matrix-unit construction, rank-one fractional-ideal argument, reduction, and invariant-subspace argument form a sufficient local proof relative to H001–H004. Carrier identity and canonical hash/transmitted-material readback are outside this mathematical judgment.\\\",\\\"checks\\\":{\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"All used premises are direct packet inputs: the prime and range assumptions support R and the unit/binomial arguments; characteristic p supports the reduction and scalar extension; H004 supplies the representation, lattice, stability, and dimension assumptions. No extra source result is invoked.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\",\\\"/inference/inputs\\\"]},\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The divided-power action formulas yield integral operators; the displayed products and unit binomial coefficients construct every matrix unit over R. Their preservation of M_R gives the coordinate-module decomposition. The finite generation, rank computation, torsion-free embedding, denominator clearing, and least-valuation generator argument establish J free of rank one. The basis actions reduce and extend to K; matrix units then send any nonzero invariant-subspace vector to every basis vector. The positive dimension handles the zero-weight case.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/logic/calculations/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"dependency_accounting\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Each H has a role in the inference: H001/H003 in localization and unit claims, H004 in the representation/lattice calculations, and H002 in reduction to K. The only substantial facts used are locally calculated or proved in the argument; no named theorem, unlisted imported result, or author-written policy is used to import one.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The argument treats an arbitrary invariant K-subspace W, shows that if it is nonzero it is the whole reduced module, and establishes the module is nonzero. This is exactly the stated irreducibility conclusion, with x,y,h invariance stronger than the x,y invariance needed in the final step.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"R,n,e_i and the operators are introduced before use; the generator a is chosen from F001 before the basis actions; W is arbitrary and r is fixed within the final step. The choice a remains inside the inference. No temporary assumption or witness escapes its scope.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no E/M sources or external applications. The direct H inputs are used at compatible parameter values; 0≤lambda<p supplies all needed bounds, and characteristic p supplies the specified residue field and scalar extension.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\",\\\"/inference/applications\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The target states the module, field, operators, and exact invariant-subspace criterion. The local F001 states the needed existence and rank-one conclusion. The proof does not rely on an equation number, absent proposition, or source crosswalk for mathematical content.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The actual objects used are parameters/primitives, input-bound objects, or local declarations with prior introduction. The indexed basis vectors, matrix units, J_i/J/Q, and generator a are declared; the only witness a is supported by the preceding local existence fact F001.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/parameters\\\",\\\"/logic/primitives\\\",\\\"/inference/locals\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"F001 is derived in S003 and used only afterward to choose a. The remaining factual steps trace to direct H inputs or the explicit local calculations. No ancestor proof or ambient premise is needed.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/10\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Sufficiency was judged from this packet alone with the Yui procedure as non-mathematical guidance. Actual mathematical input boundary: packet.json, read in full; no source proofs or other task documents. Carrier identity and canonical hash binding/transmitted-material readback are outside this mathematical review.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/packet_sha256\\\",\\\"/warning\\\",\\\"/inference/argument\\\"]}},\\\"findings\\\":[]}\"}","status":"completed"}],"error"